%S A241814 1,1,1,2,2,4,2,5,4,7,2,8,3,7,7,13,3,8,2,10,7,7,2,10,20,27,9,17,43,18,
%T A241814 2,19,4,5
%N A241814 Number of distance-regular simple connected graphs on n nodes.
%C A241814 Since the smallest distance-regular graph that is not distance-transitive is the Shrikhande graph with 16 vertices (Brouwer et al. 1989, p. 136), this counts distance transitive graphs up to and including a(15).
%C A241814 The values through a(34) are obtained from Bailey's complete list of distance-regular graphs on up to 34 vertices, including the standard families omitted from his tables. - _Vladeta Jovovic_, Sep 10 2026
%H A241814 R. F. Bailey, <a href="https://ajc.maths.uq.edu.au/pdf/62/ajc_v62_p018.pdf">The metric dimension of small distance-regular and strongly regular graphs</a>, Australas. J. Combin. 62 (2015), 18-34.
%H A241814 Travis Hoppe and Anna Petrone, <a href="https://github.com/thoppe/Encyclopedia-of-Finite-Graphs">Encyclopedia of Finite Graphs</a>
%H A241814 Travis Hoppe and Anna Petrone, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1408.3644">Integer sequence discovery from small graphs</a>, arXiv preprint arXiv:1408.3644 [math.CO], 2014.
%H A241814 Eric Weisstein's World of Mathematics, <a href="https://mathworld.wolfram.com/Distance-RegularGraph.html">Distance-Regular Graph</a>
